CSS update: `.title span {display:block}` would make title-league block, but inside line2 flex. Need override. Let's edit:
```
.title { position:relative; ...}
.title .title-line2 { display:flex; align-items:flex-end; gap:16px; margin-left:9vw; }
.title-league { margin-left:0; ...}
.title-3d { position: static; margin: 0 0 14px; ...; transform rotate(-6deg); }
```
Need remove old `.title-league margin-left:9vw`, `.title-3d position absolute...`. Also `.title span { display:block}` only direct? It applies all spans. We'll override `.title .title-line2 {display:flex}` and `.title .title-3d{display:inline-block}`. `.title-league` currently block due general. Inside flex, block okay.

Responsive `.title-league` margin-left at media 900 sets 6vw; later mobile. Need update. Add overrides:
- `@media (max-width:900px)`: `.title-line2{margin-left:6vw}`; remove title-league margin? set `.title-league{margin-left:0}`.
- max 620: `.title-line2{margin-left:4vw; gap:10px}`.
- landscape: `.title-line2{margin-left:3vw}`.

Let's patch CSS.

